class:: SDPhaseView
summary:: Language-side live phase portrait for two-output state UGens
categories:: GUI>Views
related:: Guides/StochasticDynamicsUGens, Classes/HenonMap, Classes/Chua

description::

Creates a bounded, animated two-dimensional phase trail from the first two values returned by code::stateFunction::. The same state is passed to code::soundFunction::, so a help example can visualize and sonify one UGen instance rather than an unsynchronized copy.

The server sends only code::fps:: state messages per second. The language process stores at most code::maxPoints:: coordinate pairs and performs all GUI drawing. Closing the window or pressing Cmd-period frees the Synth and OSC responder.

This is a language-side documentation and exploration utility, not a server UGen. Unlike link::Classes/ScopeView::, it displays two model coordinates against one another instead of signal amplitude against time.

classmethods::

method:: open
argument:: title
Window title.
argument:: xRange
Two-element visible range for the first state output.
argument:: yRange
Two-element visible range for the second state output.
argument:: stateFunction
Function evaluated inside the Synth graph. It must return at least two UGen signals.
argument:: soundFunction
Function receiving the state array and returning the audible graph. Nil produces silence.
argument:: fps
Display-message and animation rate, clipped to 5 through 60 frames per second.
argument:: maxPoints
Maximum retained coordinate pairs, clipped to 60 through 10,000.
returns:: An SDPhaseView instance. The server is booted automatically if necessary.

instancemethods::

method:: free
Close the window and release its Synth and responder.

examples::

code::
(
SDPhaseView.open(
    "Hénon map",
    [-1.5, 1.5],
    [-0.5, 0.5],
    { HenonMap.kr(Impulse.kr(90)) },
    { |state|
        var frequency = state[0].clip(-1.5, 1.5).linexp(-1.5, 1.5, 100, 1800);
        Pan2.ar(SinOsc.ar(frequency, 0, 0.07), state[1].clip(-0.5, 0.5) * 2)
    }
)
)
::

